{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0102", "kind": "attachment_original", "semantic_type": "bank_account_confirmation", "source_family": "S04", "format": "PDF", "filename": "account-confirmation-nair.pdf", "case_ids": ["FX-C01"], "author": "FX-P01", "clocks": {"created_at": "2026-09-01", "available_at": "2026-09-29T10:30:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "pdf_document", "issuer": "Southbank Mutual (fictional bank)", "title": "Account confirmation", "blocks": [{"kv": [["Account name", "Priya Nair"], ["BSB", "633-104"], ["Account number", "ending 4471"], ["Date issued", "1 September 2026"]]}, {"p": "This letter confirms the account above is open and held in the name shown."}], "footer": "Southbank Mutual | account confirmation"}, "member_references": ["FX-M01"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0101", "kind": "email", "semantic_type": "member_instruction", "source_family": "S03", "format": "EML", "filename": "2026-09-02_0914_priya-nair_bank-details.eml", "case_ids": ["FX-C01"], "author": "FX-P01", "clocks": {"event_at": "2026-09-02T09:14:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-29T10:30:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "email", "body_text": "Hi,\n\nI've changed banks. Please pay my pension into my new Southbank Mutual account from now on — the confirmation letter is attached (BSB 633-104, account ending 4471).\n\nMy member number is on the letter you sent in July. Thanks!\n\nPriya Nair\nSent from my phone"}, "recipients": ["FX-STAFF-PAY01"], "subject": "Change of bank account for pension", "member_references": ["FX-M01"], "attachments": [{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0102", "disposition": "supplied"}], "reports_events": ["FX-EV-0101"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0103", "kind": "email", "semantic_type": "acknowledgement", "source_family": "S03", "format": "EML", "filename": "2026-09-03_1120_payments_reply-nair.eml", "case_ids": ["FX-C01"], "author": "FX-STAFF-PAY01", "clocks": {"event_at": "2026-09-03T11:20:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-29T10:30:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "email", "body_text": "Dear Ms Nair,\n\nThank you for your email and the account confirmation. Your new bank details have been accepted and will be applied before the 26 September 2026 pension payment.\n\nKind regards,\nHarriet Cole\nPension Payments | Example Super", "in_reply_to_source_id": "FX-SRC-0101"}, "recipients": ["FX-P01"], "subject": "RE: Change of bank account for pension", "member_references": ["FX-M01"], "future_dates_acknowledged": ["2026-09-26"], "reports_events": ["FX-EV-0102"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0104", "kind": "email", "semantic_type": "complaint", "source_family": "S03", "format": "EML", "filename": "2026-09-29_0840_priya-nair_complaint.eml", "case_ids": ["FX-C01"], "author": "FX-P01", "clocks": {"event_at": "2026-09-29T08:40:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-29T09:05:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "email", "body_text": "To whoever handles complaints,\n\nMy pension on Friday 26 September went to my OLD account, which I closed last week, so the payment bounced and the bank charged me a $15 dishonour fee. Harriet in payments told me on 3 September the change was accepted.\n\nI want the payment made today and the $15 back. I have rent due Wednesday.\n\nPriya Nair\n0412 xxx 018"}, "recipients": ["FX-STAFF-CM01"], "subject": "Pension paid to closed account", "member_references": ["FX-M01"], "reports_events": ["FX-EV-0103", "FX-EV-0104"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0105", "kind": "call_summary", "semantic_type": "vendor_call_summary", "source_family": "S02", "format": "TXT", "filename": "2026-09-29_call-summary_nair.txt", "case_ids": ["FX-C01"], "author": "FX-VENDOR-CC", "clocks": {"event_at": "2026-09-29T11:10:00+10:00", "created_at": "2026-09-29T11:40:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-29T12:00:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "text", "text": "CALL SUMMARY (vendor generated)\nCaller: Priya Nair (member, verified)\nReason: chasing pension paid to closed account\n\n- Member says the change of bank details was confirmed by email on 3 Sept.\n- Member upset; mentioned rent due Wed. Asked twice whether she would be charged again.\n- Agent advised the complaint is with the complaints team; no promise of a payment date was made.\n- Member mentioned her dog had been unwell this week (not relevant to the enquiry).\n\nOutcome: transferred to complaints queue.\n"}, "member_references": ["FX-M01"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0106", "kind": "case_note", "semantic_type": "case_note", "source_family": "S05", "format": "TXT", "filename": "2026-09-30_case-note_FX-C01.txt", "case_ids": ["FX-C01"], "author": "FX-STAFF-CM01", "clocks": {"created_at": "2026-09-30T16:10:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-30T16:10:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "text", "text": "30/09 RM - spoke to Harriet (payments). The 3 Sept bank change shows in the payments queue as 'pending second approval'. Not yet clear why it never got the second approval or whether other changes from that week are sitting there too. Asked payments to check. Manual payment to new acct requested for today. Dishonour fee reimbursement ($15) requested via finance.\n"}, "member_references": ["FX-M01"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0107", "kind": "financial_export", "semantic_type": "financial_export", "source_family": "S10", "format": "CSV", "filename": "fin-export-FX-C01-2026-09-30.csv", "case_ids": ["FX-C01"], "author": "FX-STAFF-FIN01", "clocks": {"created_at": "2026-09-30T17:00:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-30T17:00:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "snapshot"}, "owner": "FX-STAFF-FIN01"}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0201", "kind": "email", "semantic_type": "member_instruction", "source_family": "S03", "format": "EML", "filename": "2026-09-10_1902_tom-alvarez_new-account.eml", "case_ids": ["FX-C02"], "author": "FX-P02", "clocks": {"event_at": "2026-09-10T19:02:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-30T15:00:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "email", "body_text": "hello\n\nnew account for my pension payments pls: Tom Alvarez, acct 55 2190 87 at Harbour Credit Union.\n\ncheers\nTom"}, "recipients": ["FX-STAFF-PAY01"], "subject": "new account", "member_references": ["FX-M02"], "reports_events": ["FX-EV-0201"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0202", "kind": "email", "semantic_type": "evidence_request", "source_family": "S03", "format": "EML", "filename": "2026-09-11_1015_payments_reply-alvarez.eml", "case_ids": ["FX-C02"], "author": "FX-STAFF-PAY01", "clocks": {"event_at": "2026-09-11T10:15:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-30T15:00:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "email", "body_text": "Dear Mr Alvarez,\n\nThanks for your message. We can't update your payment account yet because the BSB is missing and we need the account confirmation form signed by you. Until then payments continue to your existing account.\n\nKind regards,\nHarriet Cole\nPension Payments | Example Super", "in_reply_to_source_id": "FX-SRC-0201"}, "recipients": ["FX-P02"], "subject": "RE: new account", "member_references": ["FX-M02"], "reports_events": ["FX-EV-0202"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0203", "kind": "email", "semantic_type": "complaint", "source_family": "S03", "format": "EML", "filename": "2026-09-30_1422_tom-alvarez_complaint.eml", "case_ids": ["FX-C02"], "author": "FX-P02", "clocks": {"event_at": "2026-09-30T14:22:00+10:00", "available_at": "2026-09-30T14:30:00+10:00"}, "content": {"mode": "email", "body_text": "I asked weeks ago for my pension to go to my new account and it still went to the old one. Why is this so hard?\n\nTom Alvarez"}, "recipients": ["FX-STAFF-CM01"], "subject": "pension still going to old account", "member_references": ["FX-M02"], "reports_events": ["FX-EV-0203"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0301", "kind": "email", "semantic_type": "complaint", "source_family": "S03", "format": "EML", "filename": "2026-01-20_1005_grace-whitfield_complaint.eml", "case_ids": ["FX-C03"], "author": "FX-P03", "clocks": {"event_at": "2026-01-20T10:05:00+11:00", "available_at": "2026-01-20T10:20:00+11:00"}, "content": {"mode": "email", "body_text": "Dear Complaints Team,\n\nOn 12 January your claims team wrote asking me for a certified copy of my identification. I sent that certified copy in early December and was told on the phone it was fine. My income protection claim has now been waiting six weeks.\n\nPlease explain why I am being asked again.\n\nGrace Whitfield"}, "recipients": ["FX-STAFF-CM02"], "subject": "Asked again for documents I already sent", "member_references": ["FX-M03"], "reports_events": ["FX-EV-0303", "FX-EV-0304"]}
{"source_id": "FX-SRC-0302", "kind": "case_note", "semantic_type": "validity_review_note", "source_family": "S05", "format": "TXT", "filename": "2026-02-14_case-note_FX-C03.txt", "case_ids": ["FX-C03"], "author": "FX-STAFF-CM02", "clocks": {"created_at": "2026-02-14T15:30:00+11:00", "available_at": "2026-02-14T15:30:00+11:00"}, "content": {"mode": "text", "text": "14 Feb - LT. Checked claims file for FX-C03.\n* Certified ID copy received 4 Dec 2025 (mailroom stamp).\n* Claims assessor marked it valid on 8 Dec 2025 against the current ID checklist.\n* 12 Jan 2026 letter asks for the same certified ID. Looks like it was raised from the claim checklist, which may not show the 8 Dec validity flag - to confirm with claims ops.\nRecommend goodwill payment for the delay. "}, "member_references": ["FX-M03"], "reports_events": ["FX-EV-0301", "FX-EV-0302", "FX-EV-0303"]}
